verifier reproduction of AC-BASE-07 — sample-voice, no-network preload, keys unset, isolated cache
== --help
sample-voice — read one paragraph with several voices and report wpm for each

Usage: sample-voice [--voices A,B,C] [--text "..." | --text-file f] [options]

Writes <out-dir>/<voice>.wav for each voice and prints one line per voice: words,
seconds, wpm, sample rate, and whether the clip came from the cache. Needs
PEAK_MEDIA_OPENROUTER_API_KEY (legacy: TTS_OPENROUTER_API_KEY) unless --tts-model fake/tone. Clips are cached in
~/.cache/peak-media/tts/ (PEAK_MEDIA_TTS_CACHE overrides).

Options:
      --voices <list>      Comma-separated voices (Gemini names, or MAI short ids) (default: Achird,Kore,Puck)
      --text <paragraph>   Paragraph to read (default: a neutral sample paragraph)
      --text-file <file>   Read the paragraph from a file instead
      --tts-model <model>  TTS model (see references/voices.md; fake/tone for offline tests) (default: google/gemini-3.8-flash-lite-tts)
      --style <text>       Delivery style, sent as instructions (Gemini only)
      --out-dir <dir>      Where the WAVs go (default: voice-samples)
      --debug-requests     Log each OpenRouter request/response to stderr (key redacted)
      --json               Print the results as JSON instead of lines
  -h, --help               Show this help and exit
      --version            Print the plugin version and exit

Examples:
  sample-voice --voices Achird,Kore,Puck --style "Clear, friendly explainer tone."
  sample-voice --tts-model microsoft/mai-voice-2.1-flash --voices en-GB-Emily,en-US-Harper
exit=0
